    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0641" n="629" xml:id="pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12907: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-08T16:00:00+03:00">July 8, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 8—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1315. The evacuation of children from Moscow continues and the evacuation of
                    women with children has now begun. It would appear from the general preparations
                    being made that the Soviet authorities intend to defend the city against
                    attacks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
